    {
      "id": "2ac5c65c183864a3fdd5271081151c8f49750439",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1026946477,
          "type": null,
          "body": "This has been talked about extensively in the past. Most devs but also quite a lot of users are against it, because it clutters up space (especially on small laptops with multiple addresses attached to interfaces - I've seen up to 6 addresses attached to an if) and does not align properly. \n\nI do get the idea for better understanding which interface to select, but my answer would be, if you have 6-7 interfaces capturing at parallel, then you know what you are doing anyway and probably also know the devices interface name. \n\nIF (!) this may to be merged, it should be a configurable option (probably handled via context menu) and disabled by default. For that I would gladly accept it. Also, it needs to be tested beyond just ip addresses, as we have a bunch of interfaces now that have different addresses, e.g. USB or Bluetooth",
          "author": {
            "id": 2498449,
            "username": "rknall",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Roland Knall",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9e1d973c5007651b2ca47071f80324c2de5349d873e365cf0761df5542dfe382?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/rknall"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-07-14T16:28:39.924Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-07-14T16:28:39.924Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 165917389,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 7427,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "04014eb8a751d7eeac93da6eadd8cbb1914b110a",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1028110542,
          "type": null,
          "body": "We talked more in person yesterday about this, and I always appreciate your feedback.\n(I remember previous discussions about this, but couldn't find them - Maybe they were on Gerrit)\n\nI'll leave this in Draft, until I have time to figure out the preferences approach, and make it clean.\n\nI agree that it can clutter the interface, depending on number of IP addresses attached to interfaces. Some other thoughts I had to help with the clutter, but these suggestions might be more controversial:\n1. Add horizontal lines to separate the interfaces from each other, so there is more visual distinction between the IP addresses\n2. Limit the display to 1x IPv4, 1x IPv6 address.\n3. Reduce the size of the Previously Opened Pcaps List, to give more space to the Interface List.\n\nSorting the sparklines is another visual indicator to help with the same reason for this change. But, the sparklines still have some issues: https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/issues/15470 (At least on Windows, you mentioned it might be better on macOS now)",
          "author": {
            "id": 6776884,
            "username": "daulis0",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Dylan Ulis",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/c68acd7dda7fdc901223951806239c2a73929b808558dfddefbcc6fa0176ca02?s=80&d=identicon",
